# Project Vision

## Project Name

AI Newsletter Intelligence Digest

---

# Vision Statement

Design and implement an AI-powered automation system that transforms technical newsletters into actionable, personalized intelligence.

The system aims to reduce information overload by automatically identifying, classifying, and summarizing content aligned with current areas of professional interest, enabling more efficient consumption of high-value technical information.

---

# Problem Statement

Technical professionals are exposed to a continuous stream of newsletters, articles, and industry updates.

While these publications contain valuable information, manually reviewing every newsletter is time-consuming and often results in relevant content being overlooked.

The challenge is not a lack of information, but efficiently identifying the information that deserves attention.

---

# Proposed Solution

Develop an AI-powered workflow that automatically:

- Collects technical newsletters
- Extracts relevant topics
- Classifies content into predefined technical domains
- Evaluates the relevance of each topic
- Stores structured results for future reference
- Produces concise personalized digests

The objective is to support informed decision-making while minimizing the time required to remain current with rapidly evolving technologies.

---

# Professional Focus

The project demonstrates the practical application of AI and workflow automation to solve a real-world information management problem.

It emphasizes engineering practices commonly found in modern software and cybersecurity environments, including:

- AI-assisted information processing
- Workflow orchestration
- Prompt engineering
- API integration
- Structured data extraction
- Modular architecture
- Technical documentation
- Automated testing
- Continuous improvement through iterative development

---

# Design Principles

The system is designed around the following principles:

- Solve a real problem before selecting technology.
- Build incrementally using Agile practices.
- Keep the architecture modular and extensible.
- Prefer structured data over unstructured text.
- Automate repetitive decision-making where appropriate.
- Document important technical decisions.
- Validate functionality through repeatable testing.
- Design for future extensibility.

---

# Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful when it can:

- Automatically process incoming newsletters.
- Produce accurate AI-generated summaries.
- Correctly classify technical topics.
- Identify articles with high professional relevance.
- Reduce manual review effort.
- Generate concise daily or weekly intelligence digests.

---

# Long-Term Vision

The architecture is intentionally designed to support future extensions, including:

- n8n
- Local LLMs
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
- Vector databases
- Threat intelligence feeds
- RSS aggregation
- Technical blogs
- Security advisories (CISA, BSI, NIST)
- Research publications

Over time, the project may evolve into a personal AI-assisted technical intelligence platform capable of aggregating, organizing, and prioritizing information from multiple trusted sources.